Which registers contain arguments to functions? For example, which register holds 13 in main's call to printf?

In the standard RISC-V calling convention, funtion arguments are passed in the argument registers a0 ~ a7
printf passes 3 arguments  a0,a1,a2
a0 -> format string ("%d %d\n")
a1 -> result of f(8)+1 : already calculated(Constant Folding)
a3 -> 13


